# Accepted and deferred misconfigurations. Reviewed 2026-09-08.
# Every entry states why. Re-review when the infrastructure changes.

# Unrestricted egress. The monitor's purpose is reaching arbitrary
# external endpoints to check whether they respond; restricting egress
# by CIDR would defeat it. No ingress rules exist on this group.
AWS-0104

# No S3 access logging on the state bucket. Logging needs a second
# bucket, which is then flagged for the same thing. State access is
# already attributable via CloudTrail in this single-user account.
AWS-0089

# ECR uses the AWS-managed key rather than a CMK. ECR encryption is
# fixed at repository creation, so changing it means destroying the
# repository and every published image. Not worth it for key rotation
# control over public base layers.
AWS-0033

# Root EBS volume unencrypted. Fixing this replaces the instance, and
# the software on it is not yet managed as code (see README). Deferred
# until user_data provisioning lands, not accepted permanently.
AWS-0131

# SNS topic uses the AWS-managed key rather than a CMK. Terraform state
# gets a customer-managed key because it can contain secrets; alert
# payloads are hostnames and journal excerpts, where the AWS-managed key
# is proportionate. Deliberate difference, not an oversight.
AWS-0136
